{"engine":"Windows.Media.Ocr en-US","scale":3,"pages":[{"page":1,"width":2448,"height":3168,"lines":[{"text":"OFFICE OF","x":674,"y":299,"w":226,"h":37},{"text":"ASSESSOR-COUNTY CLERK-","x":674,"y":359,"w":620,"h":47},{"text":"RECORDER & ELECTIONS","x":675,"y":428,"w":549,"h":47},{"text":"COUNTY OF SAN MATEO","x":674,"y":499,"w":506,"h":38},{"text":"MARK CHURCH","x":1648,"y":353,"w":343,"h":43},{"text":"CHIEF ELECTIONS OFFICER &","x":1592,"y":407,"w":458,"h":35},{"text":"ASSESSOR-COUNTY CLERK-RECORDER","x":1522,"y":446,"w":599,"h":39},{"text":"Ballot Measure Rebuttal Argument Submission Form","x":623,"y":614,"w":1235,"h":55},{"text":"If both an argument in favor of and an argument against a measure have been selected for publication in the Sample","x":321,"y":689,"w":1821,"h":43},{"text":"Ballot & Oficial Voter Informafion Pamphlet, a typed rebuttal to the argument in favor of or the argument against the","x":321,"y":730,"w":1813,"h":43},{"text":"measure may be submitted as outlined in this form.","x":321,"y":774,"w":796,"h":36},{"text":"The author(s) of the primary argument of the measure may prepare and submit a rebuttal argument or may authorize","x":321,"y":841,"w":1822,"h":42},{"text":"in writing any other person or persons to prepare, submit or sign the rebuttal argument.","x":322,"y":883,"w":1350,"h":41},{"text":"A rebuttal argument will not be accepted unless accompanied by this completed form, which shall contain the printed","x":321,"y":952,"w":1820,"h":41},{"text":"name(s) and signature(s) of the person(s) submitting it or, if submitted on behalf of a bona fide association of citizens,","x":322,"y":994,"w":1831,"h":41},{"text":"the name of the association and the printed name and signature of at least one of its principal offcers. Please make","x":321,"y":1035,"w":1822,"h":41},{"text":"sure you are using proper format before submitting to the Elections Office.","x":322,"y":1077,"w":1249,"h":39},{"text":"Word count limit for Rebuttal Arguments = 250 words","x":321,"y":1145,"w":825,"h":38},{"text":"for the Get')","x":887,"y":1198,"w":260,"h":62},{"text":"Ballot Measure","x":324,"y":1215,"w":234,"h":30},{"text":"11/3/24","x":1784,"y":1132,"w":235,"h":119},{"text":"to be held on","x":1485,"y":1218,"w":202,"h":29},{"text":"Äebuttal to Argument Against Measure","x":1270,"y":1283,"w":680,"h":64},{"text":"Rebuttal to Argument in Favor of Measure","x":385,"y":1290,"w":653,"h":38},{"text":"Signed by Same Individual(s) Selected for the Voter Information Pamphlet for the Primary Argument","x":346,"y":1394,"w":1664,"h":39},{"text":"If the rebuttal argument is signed by the same individual(s) as those already selected for the Voter Information","x":346,"y":1480,"w":1703,"h":39},{"text":"Pamphlet for the primary argument, check the following box and skip the back side of this form.","x":346,"y":1520,"w":1476,"h":40},{"text":"Rebuttal Argument Is Signed by Same Individual(s) Selected for the Voter Information Pamphlet for the","x":456,"y":1583,"w":1597,"h":39},{"text":"Primary Argument","x":456,"y":1623,"w":282,"h":36},{"text":"Contact Person's Printed Name:","x":455,"y":1676,"w":498,"h":29},{"text":"Phone:","x":456,"y":1805,"w":108,"h":29},{"text":"Email:","x":1242,"y":1806,"w":94,"h":29},{"text":"Signed by Different Individual(s) than Individual(s) Selected for the Voter Information Pamphlet for the","x":344,"y":1943,"w":1700,"h":40},{"text":"Primary Argument","x":346,"y":1985,"w":305,"h":33},{"text":"The author(s) of the primary argument may authorize any other person or persons to sign the rebuttal argument. If","x":342,"y":2043,"w":1786,"h":43},{"text":"signers are new for the rebuttal argument, please check the following box, complete the back side of this form and","x":342,"y":2083,"w":1773,"h":41},{"text":"attach the written authorization (the Authorization Form for Change in Signers of Rebutal Argument) from the","x":342,"y":2123,"w":1701,"h":44},{"text":"primary argument author(s).","x":343,"y":2164,"w":434,"h":37},{"text":"Rebuttal Argument Is Signed by New Signers as Authorized by Primary Argument Author(s)","x":453,"y":2232,"w":1423,"h":45},{"text":"Contact Person's Printed Name:","x":451,"y":2295,"w":501,"h":30},{"text":"W, A. I-finkle","x":679,"y":2339,"w":371,"h":70},{"text":"Arguments will be emailed to the contact person listed","x":335,"y":2578,"w":917,"h":36},{"text":"Ballot & Official Voter Information Pamphlets.","x":857,"y":2618,"w":760,"h":40},{"text":"Please complete the reverse side of this form.","x":856,"y":2680,"w":765,"h":37},{"text":"40 Tower Road, San Mateo, CA 94402","x":907,"y":2731,"w":661,"h":40},{"text":"P 650.312.5222 F 650.312.5348 email registrar@smcacre.gov web www.smcacre.gov","x":479,"y":2778,"w":1520,"h":46},{"text":"ample","x":2040,"y":2585,"w":104,"h":36}]},{"page":2,"width":2448,"height":3168,"lines":[{"text":"Rebuttal to Argument in Favor of Measure V","x":786,"y":332,"w":850,"h":50},{"text":"\"WITHOUT RAISING TAXES BY A PENNY\"? DON'T BE FOOLED.","x":314,"y":459,"w":1235,"h":43},{"text":"Measure V authorizes IN NEW DEBT, costing taxpayers ANNUALLY","x":313,"y":582,"w":1749,"h":52},{"text":"for the next 20+ years to pay off, Proponents call that \"simply continuing the current tax rate.\" Just","x":311,"y":640,"w":1764,"h":56},{"text":"think what else county taxpayers could fund with $75,000,000 annually instead!","x":310,"y":700,"w":1430,"h":55},{"text":"PREVIOUS BONDS TOTALING $1 ALREADY SPENT, YET BUILDINGS \"HAVE","x":313,"y":826,"w":1709,"h":51},{"text":"NEVER BEEN UPDATED\"?","x":312,"y":891,"w":516,"h":39},{"text":"Where did the $1,100,000,000 go? Hundreds of millions were spent on luxury health clubs, event","x":310,"y":1013,"w":1773,"h":56},{"text":"facilities and costly new construction, not repairs.","x":310,"y":1077,"w":884,"h":51},{"text":"Voters beware - this Bond includes another health club and costly projects far removed from","x":310,"y":1201,"w":1672,"h":53},{"text":"promised modernized classrooms for career training.","x":313,"y":1263,"w":947,"h":50},{"text":"This bond has ZERO impact on whether the colleges can continue providing quality, affordable","x":310,"y":1386,"w":1713,"h":53},{"text":"higher education; it funds capital projects.","x":313,"y":1447,"w":748,"h":50},{"text":"THEY HAVE ENOUGH MONEY FOR REPAIRS!","x":312,"y":1574,"w":876,"h":39},{"text":"During the past decade District property tax revenues have increased by $100,000,000 which they","x":314,"y":1696,"w":1778,"h":54},{"text":"should use to fund \"basic repairs\" vs. adding new bond taxes!!","x":313,"y":1756,"w":1113,"h":50},{"text":"WHO'S PAYING FOR ALL THOSE GLOSSY \"YES\" MAILERS?","x":311,"y":1883,"w":1165,"h":42},{"text":"Virtually all campaign contributions come from construction and building-related interests that","x":312,"y":2009,"w":1674,"h":53},{"text":"benefit from taxpayer-funded projects, preferring costly new buildings, not repair and","x":312,"y":2067,"w":1515,"h":50},{"text":"modernization. Coincidence or \"PAY-TO-PLAY\"?","x":312,"y":2125,"w":887,"h":42},{"text":"That \"independent oversight\"? Many on the Board-appointed committee come from building and","x":310,"y":2250,"w":1776,"h":52},{"text":"construction-related backgrounds. The committee reviews expenditures after the fact and has no","x":310,"y":2309,"w":1739,"h":49},{"text":"say in choosing which projects get funded. And, NOT TRUE, that funds can't be used for staff","x":310,"y":2366,"w":1682,"h":51},{"text":"salaries.","x":310,"y":2427,"w":148,"h":39},{"text":"FILED","x":1647,"y":2519,"w":95,"h":34},{"text":"NEW DEBT. CONTINUED TAXES. SAME BROKEN S OF THE CHIEF ELECTIONS OFFICER","x":313,"y":2552,"w":1747,"h":54},{"text":"Vote NO on Measure V","x":310,"y":2681,"w":435,"h":39},{"text":"SAN MATEO COUNTY","x":1524,"y":2616,"w":348,"h":38},{"text":"AUG 1 8 2026","x":1572,"y":2729,"w":262,"h":54},{"text":"14","x":2209,"y":1206,"w":60,"h":59},{"text":"14","x":2201,"y":1389,"w":59,"h":57},{"text":"14s","x":2186,"y":1691,"w":67,"h":62},{"text":"12",